P is not liable for murder because he did not physically enter the shop or fire the fatal shot;
Section 3(5) requires each accused to directly commit every physical element of the offence
for liability to attach.

The conviction under Section 190 is valid because the original charge involved five persons;
subsequent acquittals do not affect applicability since the assembly was lawfully constituted
when the offence occurred.

A living will executed by a family member is valid if the patient had orally authorised it;
oral authorisation satisfies the requirement of personal consent when independent
testimony corroborates it.
